Key Observations (Very Important)

Odd number rule
👉 A number is odd only if its last digit is odd (1,3,5,7,9)

Largest number rule
👉 Among valid odd substrings, the largest value will be:

The longest possible substring

Ending at the rightmost odd digit

Starting from the first non-zero digit

Leading zeroes are NOT allowed

-----------------------------
Optimal Strategy

Find the last odd digit in the string

From the start, skip all leading '0'

Return the substring between:

first non-zero index

last odd digit index

If no odd digit exists → return ""
-------------------------
class Solution {
    public String largestOddNumber(String s) {
        int n = s.length();

        // Step 1: Find last odd digit
        int lastOddIndex = -1;
        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            int digit = s.charAt(i) - '0';
            if (digit % 2 == 1) {
                lastOddIndex = i;
                break;
            }
        }

        // No odd digit found
        if (lastOddIndex == -1) return "";

        // Step 2: Find first non-zero digit
        int start = 0;
        while (start <= lastOddIndex && s.charAt(start) == '0') {
            start++;
        }

        // If all digits before odd index are zeros
        if (start > lastOddIndex) return "";

        return s.substring(start, lastOddIndex + 1);
    }
}
